WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.764
FirstClub's members get rewards in at least six places across the app.

2
00:00:05.114 --> 00:00:06.748
Its one game, Toss & Win,

3
00:00:06.748 --> 00:00:09.623
sits in the Profile menu. For a new member,

4
00:00:09.623 --> 00:00:12.890
it opens to an empty screen with nothing to play.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.822
This was a 24 hour design challenge,

6
00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:26.949
and my audit of the live app found the same pattern everywhere.

7
00:00:27.299 --> 00:00:30.656
Nearly every reward asked members for something first,

8
00:00:30.656 --> 00:00:32.894
a toss can land on the losing side,

9
00:00:32.894 --> 00:00:36.747
and nothing gave people a reason to come back between orders.

10
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:40.065
Plenty of rewards.

11
00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.377
No reason to come back tomorrow.

12
00:00:44.767 --> 00:00:47.822
I compared four places for a daily reward on Home,

13
00:00:47.822 --> 00:00:50.266
and picked the one members already use.

14
00:00:50.616 --> 00:00:55.179
A small wax seal appears on the gift icon only when there's one to open,

15
00:00:55.179 --> 00:00:58.094
and the old Toss & Win row still leads there.

16
00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:06.657
The seal comes from FirstClub's own Approved stamp. Opening one takes a press and hold for under a second.

17
00:01:07.007 --> 00:01:08.905
A ring fills, the seal cracks,

18
00:01:08.905 --> 00:01:11.690
and there's always something useful inside,

19
00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.474
with nothing to buy first and no countdown.

20
00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.615
Instead of a streak that resets,

21
00:01:18.615 --> 00:01:21.332
any five seals in a week earn a Golden Seal,

22
00:01:21.332 --> 00:01:23.122
and members choose the gift.

23
00:01:23.472 --> 00:01:26.222
Rewards then apply on their own in the cart,

24
00:01:26.222 --> 00:01:28.097
with nothing extra to unlock.

25
00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.458
In a day, I delivered the audit, the main flow,

26
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:37.355
nine edge cases and a clickable prototype, built with AI.

27
00:01:37.705 --> 00:01:38.599
It isn't built,

28
00:01:38.599 --> 00:01:43.548
so next I'd test the hold with members and measure orders against a holdout group.

29
00:01:46.433 --> 00:01:49.326
Most of the work was finding what the app already had,

30
00:01:49.326 --> 00:01:50.344
and connecting it.
